# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Price Tracker — frontend (Expo) environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. Everything here is optional; the app runs with no configuration.
#
# Expo only exposes variables prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ to app code, and they are INLINED INTO THE
# BUNDLE at build time — so treat every value here as public and never put a secret in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backend location -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the app sends its search requests. Leave unset and `utils/constant.ts` picks a sensible
# default per platform: http://localhost:5000 on web and iOS, http://10.0.2.2:5000 on the Android
# emulator (which maps the host machine to that address).
#
# A PHYSICAL device needs this set explicitly — `localhost` there means the phone itself, so point
# it at your machine's LAN address, e.g. http://192.168.1.20:5000
EXPO_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=

# --- Fallback delivery location ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Used only when the device refuses a position — a declined browser prompt, or location services
# off. Quick commerce is hyperlocal, so a search with no coordinates cannot be answered at all; the
# UI always labels results as coming from this fallback rather than pretending otherwise.
#
# Set these to a city your deployment actually serves. The built-in defaults (Gurugram Sector 45)
# exist so a fresh clone demonstrates a working app, not because that location is special.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_LATITUDE=28.4419
EXPO_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_LONGITUDE=77.0658
EXPO_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_ADDRESS_TEXT=Sector 45, Gurugram
EXPO_PUBLIC_FALLBACK_PINCODE=122003
